    state_N + grammar_vG
      -> run the tournament (mb_sim, fixed seeds, pinned config)
      -> detect situations, compute score(state_N)
      -> emit candidate patches from the highest-priority situations
      -> state_N+1 = state_N + patch  (as an OVERLAY, never a write)
      -> re-run, re-score
      -> ACCEPT on strict improvement; else REJECT and take the next candidate

HARD RULE: `data/` is never edited during a run. Every evaluation loads the
canonical data plus the overlay stack in memory; the canonical files are
written only by an explicit `--apply` at the end, through the same textual
leaf replacement the solve staging uses.

RESOLUTION PURITY. When candidates get re-solved, the BASE is re-solved too,
at the same profile, once at run start -- a supplied policy directory's
resolution is unknown, and a comparison is sound only when every state in it
was solved the same way. At profile `skip` nothing is re-solved anywhere, so
the comparison stays symmetric the other way.
